Multichar_Symbols +V @P.PREF.Ma@

! ma- as prefix (historic: building statives in Polynesian languages, not yet productive)

LEXICON root
@P.PREF.Ma@ma MaTerms ; ! for verbs which allow the ma-prefix (separate lexicon)
              MaTerms ; ! ... for making the prefix optional

LEXICON MaTerms
hora VTag ; ! V: "to spread out, display, make public" -> mahora V: "be spread out, laid out, served up"
tika VTag ; ! V: "to be correct, true, upright" -> matika V: "to stand, rise to an erect position"

LEXICON VTag
+V:0   #;

! ---------------------------------------------
! cd .../xfsm_api/linux64/bin/
! ./xfst
! read lexc .../blocks/ma-Prefix.xfst
! print upper-words; print lower-words
